<speak>That is fine. I will look at the diary at home rather than guessing from memory. My wife may already have put something into the week that I have forgotten to copy over. We are trying to keep a little more personal time free, especially before the family visit. It is very easy for me to say yes to an office meeting and then realise I have used the only quiet afternoon we had. I am learning to check first. It sounds like a small thing, but it saves an unnecessary discussion at the dinner table when our calendars do not match.</speak>